# chktex configuration for this conjecture. Run from this directory:
#
#     chktex -q statement.tex
#
# One warning is suppressed, checked hit by hit on 28 August 2026 rather
# than assumed, with a 100% false-positive rate in this file:
#
#   38  "You should not use punctuation in front of quotes." Each of the 4
#       hits is the final character of a sentence quoted verbatim from the
#       source paper. The punctuation belongs to the quoted text; moving it
#       outside the quotation marks would misquote the source.  (4 hits)
#
# Everything else stays on, and the four other warnings chktex raised on
# the first drafts were fixed in the source rather than silenced: one
# warning 1 (a space inside the \ket macro), one warning 8 (an en-dash in
# "Porter--Thomas", where the house style writes a plain hyphen), and two
# warning 40 hits on "$t!$", which lacheck flagged too and which are now
# written out as "t factorial". As of 28 August 2026 the file is clean
# under this config and `lacheck statement.tex` is silent.

CmdLine
{
    -n38
}
